+<!-- ─── FILE SYSTEM ENDPOINTS ─── -->
+<div class="api-section-title">File System Endpoints</div>
+
+<p style="font-size:0.92em;color:#444;">File system operations are exposed by
+<a href="#/modules/FSRESTModuleImpl">FSRESTModuleImpl</a> under the session-scoped namespace <code>/agent/sessions/{sessionToken}/fs</code>.
+A session is required, exactly as on the SOAP interface, whose endpoint is published behind the session filter: open one with <code>POST /agent/sessions</code> and the page fills the token in everywhere. File operations do not otherwise use the session.
+Paths are passed URL-encoded in the <code>path</code> query parameter (the page encodes them for you).
+File content travels as raw <code>application/octet-stream</code> bodies; everything else is JSON.
+<code>GET /agent/sessions/{sessionToken}/fs/entries</code> never returns 404 — <code>"exists": false</code> is the answer.</p>
+
+<!-- GET /agent/sessions/{sessionToken}/fs/entries -->
+<div class="api-endpoint" data-id="fs-stat">
+  <div class="api-endpoint-header get">
+    <span class="method-badge get">GET</span>
+    <span class="api-endpoint-path">/agent/sessions/{sessionToken}/fs/entries?path=</span>
+    <span class="api-endpoint-desc">Existence, type and size</span>
+    <span class="api-endpoint-chevron">▶</span>
+  </div>
+  <div class="api-endpoint-body">
+    <p style="margin:0 0 12px;font-size:0.92em;color:#444;">Reports whether the path exists, whether it is a <code>file</code> or <code>directory</code>, and for a readable file its <code>size</code>. SOAP equivalents: <code>fileExists</code>, <code>directoryExists</code>, <code>fileSize</code>.</p>
+    <div class="api-field-group">
+      <label>sessionToken <span class="api-required">required</span></label>
+      <input type="text" data-param="sessionToken" placeholder="paste session token here">
+    </div>
+    <div class="api-field-group">
+      <label>path <span class="api-required">required</span></label>
+      <div class="field-hint">Absolute path on the Remote Agent host</div>
+      <input type="text" data-param="path" placeholder="/tmp/example.txt">
+    </div>
+    <button class="api-execute-btn">Execute</button>
+    <div class="api-curl-label">curl</div>
+    <div class="api-curl-preview" data-curl></div>
+    <div class="api-response-panel"><div class="api-response-header">Response <span class="api-status-badge pending" data-status></span></div><div class="api-response-body" data-body></div></div>
+  </div>
+</div>
+
+<!-- GET /agent/sessions/{sessionToken}/fs/files -->
+<div class="api-endpoint" data-id="fs-read">
+  <div class="api-endpoint-header get">
+    <span class="method-badge get">GET</span>
+    <span class="api-endpoint-path">/agent/sessions/{sessionToken}/fs/files?path=[&amp;offset=&amp;length=]</span>
+    <span class="api-endpoint-desc">Read a file</span>
+    <span class="api-endpoint-chevron">▶</span>
+  </div>
+  <div class="api-endpoint-body">
+    <p style="margin:0 0 12px;font-size:0.92em;color:#444;">Returns the file content as <code>application/octet-stream</code>. Omit <code>length</code> for the whole file (<code>413</code> above <code>maxFileSize</code>); give <code>offset</code>/<code>length</code> to read a window. <code>404</code> if not a file, <code>403</code> if not readable. SOAP equivalents: <code>readEntireFile</code>, <code>readFile</code>.</p>
+    <div class="api-field-group">
+      <label>sessionToken <span class="api-required">required</span></label>
+      <input type="text" data-param="sessionToken" placeholder="paste session token here">
+    </div>
+    <div class="api-field-group">
+      <label>path <span class="api-required">required</span></label>
